       PROCESS OPTIONS NOFS21DUPKEY
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.                       TCODERNM.
       AUTHOR.                           A.M.TREUDLER.
       DATE-WRITTEN.                     JAN. 1988.
       DATE-COMPILED.                    CURRENT-DATE.
      *REMARKS.
      *C  25JUN92        DAVE PLUM      REQUEST #6225
      *C  MADE SOME MINOR CHANGES TO THE MOVE STATEMENTS USED TO
      *C  SET UP THE TC-311 AND TC-411 RECORDS PRIOR TO THEIR BEING
      *C  WRITTEN TO DATASET DDAILYTC.  SPECIFICALLY, FOR TC-311 ID 4
      *C  NOTHING WAS BEING MOVED TO FIELD TC311-REORDER.  THEREFORE,
      *C  THIS NUMERIC FIELD ENDED UP WITH SPACES IN IT.  THE PROPER
      *C  REORDER VALUE WILL NOW BE MOVED TO THE TC-311 RECORD FROM
      *C  DATASET MSTORERM.
      *C
      *C  08/24/92  BK DISMUKES  REQUEST 6252
      *C    1. ADDED LOGIC TO RENAME RESTRICTION TABLE IF REQUIRED.
      *C     A.IF OLD CODE IS RESTRICTED AND NEW CODE IS NOT - THE
      *C       NEW CODE TAKES THE OLD CODES RESTRICTIONS.
      *C     B.IF NEW CODE IS RESTRICTED - NEW CODE KEEPS
      *C       CURRENT RESTRICTIONS REGARDLESS OF OLD CODES STATUS.
      *C     C.IF NEITHER OLD OR NEW CODE HAS RESTRICTIONS -
      *C       NOTHING IS DONE REGARDING RESTRICTION TABLES.
      *C
      *C  09/14/93 JS BUNGO     REQUEST 6420
      *C  ADD CALL TO SJOBPCOD TO RENAME THE CODE IN MMISA PM-JOBPLAN
      *C  FOR THE CODE BEING RENAMED.
      *C
      *C  09/20/93  JS BUNGO    REQUEST 5643.
      *C  ADDED CALL TO SCCLKCHG TO RENAME THE CODE IN MMISA
      *C  CORP-CODE-LINK AND CC-NOTE-MSTR FOR THE CODE BEING RENAMED.
      *C
      *C  06DEC1993   DAVE PLUM
      *C  HAD TO RECOMPILE WITH GENERATION OPTIONS "*NOFS21DUPKY" SINCE
      *C  THIS PROGRAM READS FILE DPOITEM USING CORPORATE CODE AS THE KEY,
      *C  AND THEN ATTEMPTS TO CHANGE THIS KEY AND REWRITE THE RECORD.
      *C  (WITHOUT THIS OPTION A FILE-STATUS=21 ERROR OCCURRED ON THE REWRITE
      *C  STATEMENT IN PARAGRAPH 6501-GPD-DPOITEM IN TOPEKA ON 03DEC1993.)
      *C
      *C  UPON RECOMPILING, AN ERROR WAS FOUND WITHIN PARAGRAPH
      *C  640-COPY-MSTORERM.  HAD TO ADD AN "END-WRITE" STATEMENT TO
      *C  ELIMINATE THE ERROR.
      *C
      *C  01/27/1994  JEFF BUNGO
      *C  ADDED CALL TO SUBROUTINE SCCALTCH TO RENAME THE CODE FOR
      *C  AN ALTERNATE KEY, IF THE OLD CODE HAD AN ALTERNATE KEY.
      *C
      *C  07FEB1994    DAVE PLUM
      *C    ADDED CALL TO THE COBOL ERROR HANDLER - MCXCBLERR.
      *C
      *C  14JUN1996    CA YODER
      *C    FIXED PROBLEM WITH UPDATE OF DSHIPREL.  IT WASN'T BEING
      *C    CHANGED BECAUSE A START WAS NEVER PERFORMED ON THE FILE,
      *C    AND SO THE RECORD WAS NEVER FOUND.
      *C
      *C    ALSO MODIFIED PROGRAM FOR DATABASE CENTURY CHANGES.
      *C
      *C  09/26/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C    RENAME ENTRIES FROM DRCVCORR.  JUST DELETE THE ENTRIES
      *C    FROM DCHATNO SINCE THIS DATASET IS DOWNLOADED DAILY.
      *C
      *C   1/14/97    BILL ROXBURY REQ #95-012
      *C     CHANGE ENTRIES FROM IN RECEIVING FILE (MCFLCSRCPT).
      *C
      *C  10/27/1997        CA YODER
      *C    RE-COMPILED PROGRAM TO PICK UP NOTIFY USER-ID IN DSHIPREL.
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C
      *C  10/12/00    JIM COFFMAN
      *C     ADDED CODING TO HANDLE DELETING OLD CORPORATE CODES
      *C     FROM 'ITOV' PURCHASE ORDERS INSTEAD OF RENAMING THEM.
      *C     LAWTON HAD TRIED TO ORDER ITEMS AFTER THE RENAME
      *C     AND THE NEWLY RENAMED CODE ON THE 'ITOV' HAD NOT BEEN
      *C     RENAMED AT THE 'ITOV"-ISSUING PLANT AS WELL. JIM
      *C     JEFFERS THOUGHT IT BEST TO DELETE THE CODE FROM THE
      *C     'ITOV' INSTEAD OF LEAVING THE OLD CODE SITTING ON
      *C     THE SYSTEM. THIS CHANGE ONLY AFFECTS CORPORATE CODES
      *C     ON 'ITOV' PURCHASE ORDERS DURING THE RENAME PROCESS.
      *C
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
